<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Ritom–Cadagno–Tom lake circuit — Piora–Föisc–Ritom–Tom–Cadagno circuit [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Piora upper-station forecourt, climb Föisc, descend east to Ritom, follow its north shore with the Alpe Ritom spur, then visit Tom and Cadagno. Return via Alpe Piora, Fontanella and Ritom’s south-shore educational path. Plan roughly 16 km and 5.5 hours, with approximate climbing figures. The funicular is closed for renewal, with spring 2027 reopening planned. Walking through station works and driving access are unconfirmed: ask the operator before travelling. Use snow-free conditions and protect wetlands.

